= Inductive bias — Technical =

== Hypothesis selection ==
Given finite sample S, many hypotheses may achieve similar empirical risk.

A learning algorithm defines preferences among them through:

<pre>
H
regularization
prior
optimization trajectory
architecture
data augmentation
</pre>

Those preferences constitute inductive structure.

== Explicit and implicit bias ==
Explicit bias appears in penalties, priors, or hard constraints.

Implicit bias can arise from optimization algorithms or parameterization even when the explicit objective admits many equivalent solutions.

== Generalization ==
The usefulness of an inductive bias depends on alignment between the bias and the data-generating/task structure.

No single bias dominates across all possible learning problems.

